== 9. Trust points (steps where checking was not possible) ==
  T1 bootstrap: the KMS key is trusted by its RFC 7638 kid + the self-signed history document;
     the root of trust is the key first deployed 2026-09-04 (not_before_note), out of band.
  T2 the shell is unsigned (unsigned: true): amount_gross/amount_settled/pay_to/payment_tx are
     not covered by any public signature. /preimage says "payload_hash is over the owner-held bytes".
     The economic facts are corroborated on-chain instead (check-chain.sh, two RPCs).
  T3 leaf = SHA256(0x00 || task_id|row_hash); row_hash is owner-view only (shell.ts), so the
     task_id -> leaf binding is NOT recomputable from public material. The inclusion endpoint
     asserts it (task_id + leaf agree); no public attestation is served on this shell.
  T4 the anchor is a self-send (to == from == anchor wallet) whose calldata is the raw 32-byte
     root: nothing on chain validates the calldata format. The anchor wallet is the trust point.
  T5 on-chain facts rest on public Base RPCs (two independent providers agree).
  T6 the solana anchor is pending (day_already_anchored); its prior_signature is not checked here.
  T7 my fold/JCS/ES256 implementations are cross-checked against published values (entry_hash,
     fold->root); an implementation bug shared with the issuer would not be caught.
